  "description": "OBEVEB crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H98 N6 O32 Tb8. From the CIF bond table, Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb8 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.626-4.034 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.45-115.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C72H96N6O32Tb8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
